THE DRAGON IS NOT CARGO

Duration: 5seconds
Aspect Ratio: 9:16 cinematic
FPS: 48
Genre: Deep-sea techno-myth / panic descent
Energy Curve: Immediate spike → sustained dread → catastrophic release

HARD TIMING LAW (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

❌ NO scene ≥ 2.0s
✅ Most scenes 0.4–0.9s
❌ No pauses, no holds
❌ No establishing shots
If motion ever stops → INVALID
If any shot exceeds 2.0s → INVALID

AUDIO DNA (IMPLIED, NOT LITERAL)
Low-frequency BOOM… BOOM… BOOM…
Tempo: slow, ominous, heartbeat-like
Each BOOM = a cut or physical impact
Silence between beats feels pressurized, not calm
Viewer feels impending cardiac overload

RULE ZERO (ABSOLUTE)
❌ NO STATIC
❌ NO STABLE CAMERA
❌ NO FULL REVEALS
❌ NO SAFE DISTANCE

Camera is inside the incident, always late, always correcting.

CORE IDEA (LOCKED)
The submarine is moving.
The dragon is moving with it.
The crew realizes too late:
the dragon is not cargo — it is choosing to ride.

CAMERA LAW
FPV / hull-adjacent / cockpit-adjacent only
Constant micro-jitter + pressure vibration
Whip-pans caused by mass shifts, not intention
Camera reacts to weight, drag, impact

PHYSICS & MATERIALITY
Water is dense, heavy, resistant
Rust flakes shear off hull during motion
Dragon claws grind metal → sparks underwater
Pressure pulses visible as refractive shockwaves
Dragon flesh behaves like armored stone + muscle

